<tr>
<td><a target="_blank" href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/23/when-prevention-fails-we-use-criminal-law-enforcement/" rel="noopener"><img decoding="async" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Tsyvinskyi-head-of-BEB-Ukraine-682x1024.jpg"></a></td>
<td><a target="_blank" href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/23/when-prevention-fails-we-use-criminal-law-enforcement/" rel="noopener"><strong>“When prevention fails, we use law enforcement”—Ukraine’s new BEB director on fighting the $ 24 bn shadow economy</strong></a>. In his first interview since taking office, Tsyvinskyi explains how the Bureau of Economic Security will use neural networks to track laundered money from economic crimes.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<figure class="table">
<table border="0">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><a target="_blank" href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/23/if-the-eu-builds-its-drone-wall-how-might-it-actually-look/" rel="noopener"><img decoding="async" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/russian-orion-drone-moments-before-downing-300x154.jpg"></a></td>
<td><a target="_blank" href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/23/if-the-eu-builds-its-drone-wall-how-might-it-actually-look/" rel="noopener"><strong>The EU’s “drone wall” needs Ukraine’s know-how, EU cash — and integration no one owns</strong></a>.</td>
</tr>
