			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Performance marketing explained</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/23/performance-marketing-explained/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Serhii Omelchenko]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 23 Sep 2025 20:26:12 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Rundown]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=361634</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Performance marketing shifts the focus from potential reach to tangible outcomes, ensuring accountability and maximizing return on investment (ROI)]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="1024" height="717" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Performance-marketing-explained-1024x717.webp" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="Performance marketing explained" decoding="async" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Performance-marketing-explained-1024x717.webp 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Performance-marketing-explained-300x210.webp 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Performance-marketing-explained-380x266.webp 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Performance-marketing-explained-800x560.webp 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Performance-marketing-explained-1160x812.webp 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Performance-marketing-explained.webp 1280w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    
<p></p>


<p>In the digital advertising landscape, where every dollar of marketing spend is under scrutiny, performance marketing has emerged as a crucial strategy for growth-focused brands. Unlike traditional advertising that often focuses on broad awareness, performance marketing is a results-driven approach where advertisers only pay when a specific, measurable action is completed. This simple premise, “pay for what works,” solves the age-old marketing dilemma famously captured by the quote, “Half the money I spend on advertising is wasted; the trouble is I don’t know which half”.</p>
<p><a target="_blank" href="https://www.mgid.com/blog/performance-marketing-explained" rel="noopener">Performance marketing</a> shifts the focus from potential reach to tangible outcomes, ensuring accountability and maximizing return on investment (ROI).</p>
<h2 id="core-principles-and-payment-models">Core principles and payment models</h2>
<p>The core of performance marketing is its focus on measurable results. It is a transactional and immediate strategy that contrasts with brand marketing, which aims to build long-term perception and loyalty. Advertisers collaborate with publishers and marketing platforms, agreeing to pay based on the successful completion of desired actions.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>
<p>Key payment models in performance marketing include:</p>
<ul>
<li aria-level="1">Cost Per Click (CPC) Advertisers pay for each click on their advertisement.</li>
<li aria-level="1">Cost Per Lead (CPL) Payment is triggered when a user signs up or provides their contact information, generating a new lead.</li>
<li aria-level="1">Cost Per Acquisition (CPA) Also known as Cost Per Sale (CPS), advertisers pay only when a click leads directly to a sale or conversion.</li>
<li aria-level="1">Cost Per Install (CPI) Primarily used for mobile apps, payment is made each time a user installs the application.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="key-channels-in-performance-marketing">Key channels in performance marketing</h2>
<p>Performance marketing utilizes a variety of digital channels to reach audiences and drive actions.</p>
<ul>
<li aria-level="1">Native Advertising This channel involves integrating ads seamlessly into the surrounding content of a website or app, creating a non-intrusive user experience that enhances engagement. Global platforms specializing in native advertising empower advertisers to connect with the right audience through advanced targeting options and real-time analytics, distributing their message across a vast network of publishers.</li>
<li aria-level="1">Affiliate Marketing One of the earliest forms of performance marketing, affiliate marketing involves partners promoting a product or service in exchange for a commission on the sales or leads they generate.</li>
<li aria-level="1">Search Engine Marketing (SEM) This involves placing paid ads on search engine results pages (SERPs) and typically operates on a CPC basis, targeting users based on their search queries.</li>
<li aria-level="1">Social Media Advertising Platforms like Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn offer sophisticated tools for running performance-based campaigns, allowing advertisers to target users based on demographics, interests, and behaviors.</li>
</ul><div data-fuse="incontent_2"></div>
<h2 id="benefits-of-a-performance-based-strategy">Benefits of a performance-based strategy</h2>
<p>Adopting a performance marketing approach offers businesses several distinct advantages.</p>
<h3 id="measurable-roi-and-low-risk"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Measurable ROI and low risk</span></h3>
<p>The most significant benefit is the ability to track and measure the ROI of every campaign with precision. Because payment is tied directly to results, the financial risk for advertisers is significantly reduced. This data-driven model allows for transparent budget allocation and a clear understanding of what tactics are driving success.</p>
<h3 id="advanced-targeting-and-optimization"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Advanced targeting and optimization</span></h3><div data-fuse="incontent_3"></div>
<p>Performance marketing thrives on data. Sophisticated platforms provide advertisers with in-depth targeting capabilities, allowing them to segment audiences based on geography, device, browser, and user behavior. This ensures that ads are shown to the users most likely to convert. Furthermore, real-time analytics enable continuous campaign optimization, allowing marketers to make data-based decisions to improve tactics and maximize ROI.</p>
<h3 id="brand-safety-and-user-re-engagement"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Brand safety and user re-engagement</span></h3>
<p>Leading platforms prioritize brand safety, utilizing proprietary fraud-prevention systems to protect brand integrity. Additionally, performance marketing includes powerful retargeting strategies to re-engage users who have previously shown interest in a brand, guiding them further down the funnel toward a conversion.</p>
<p>By focusing on measurable outcomes, leveraging diverse digital channels, and utilizing advanced technology platforms, performance marketing offers a powerful and efficient way for brands to achieve their business objectives in 2025 and beyond.</p>


<p></p>

        <div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1805850"></div>
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    ]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<enclosure url="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Performance-marketing-explained-1024x717.webp" length="65044" type="image/webp" />	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Trump says Ukraine can reclaim its territory from Russia &#8220;with time&#8221; — but Kyiv urgently needs 60 billions to fight in 2026</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/23/trump-says-ukraine-can-reclaim-its-territory-from-russia-with-time-but-kyiv-urgently-needs-60-billions-to-fight-in-2026/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Olena Mukhina]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 23 Sep 2025 20:18:18 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Latest news Ukraine]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=361847</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[As Trump says patience will lead Ukraine to the success, Moscow is arming itself with lifelines from China and North Korea each day. ]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="640" height="427" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Trump_at_the_NATO_Summit_2025_June_24_2025.jpg" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="US President Donald Trump at the 2025 NATO summit." decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Trump_at_the_NATO_Summit_2025_June_24_2025.jpg 640w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Trump_at_the_NATO_Summit_2025_June_24_2025-300x200.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Trump_at_the_NATO_Summit_2025_June_24_2025-380x254.jpg 380w" sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    <p data-start="51" data-end="191"><strong data-start="51" data-end="189">US President Donald Trump says Ukraine has every chance to reclaim all territory “with time,” patience, and support from the EU and NATO. </strong>Meanwhile, Ukraine needs weapons and billions of dollars to defend itself from Moscow, backed by China and North Korea. </p>
<div class="pk-content-block pk-block-bg pk-block-bg-light" data-start="225" data-end="603">
<p>Since taking office, Trump has not approved military aid packages for Ukraine and has not imposed sanctions on Russia. At the same time, Moscow’s terror<strong> has escalated each time</strong> after the US president talked or met with Russian ruler Vladimir Putin, which ended with <strong>Ukrainian civilians being killed. </strong></p>
</div>
<p data-start="870" data-end="913">Earlier, Trump claimed he could end the war in Ukraine in <strong>24 hours</strong>. However, nine months later, this has not happened.</p>
<p data-start="870" data-end="913">In addition, Secretary of State Marco Rubio noted that the US decision not to impose sanctions on Russia for escalating terror against civilians reflects a deliberate US policy acting as a broker between Ukraine and Russia. Yet the war has not ended. Moreover, <strong>the Russian attacks continued not only in Ukraine but also in Poland. </strong></p><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>
<p data-start="870" data-end="913">In September, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy stated that if the war continues into 2026, the country will lack $120 billion annually to finance defense and recovery. </p>
<p data-start="0" data-end="80">Half of this sum<span style="margin: 0px;padding: 0px">—$60 billion—<a target="_blank" href="https://t.me/V_Zelenskiy_official/16121" rel="noopener">comes</a></span> from Ukraine’s budget, while <strong>another $60 billion must be secured from other sources, primarily Western partners.</strong></p>
<h3 id="trump-on-russias-war-against-ukraine" data-start="870" data-end="913">Trump on Russia’s war against Ukraine</h3>
<p data-start="915" data-end="1109">Trump’s statements <a target="_blank" href="https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/115255130298104593" rel="noopener">came</a> after the UN. On 23 September 2025, Donald Trump was in New York, where he met with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on the sidelines of the UN General Assembly.</p>
<p data-start="1111" data-end="1374">In a post on Truth Social, Trump said that after reviewing the military and economic situation in Ukraine and Russia, he believes Ukraine, with support from the EU, is in a position to fight and reclaim all its territory within its original borders.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_2"></div>
<blockquote>
<p data-start="1376" data-end="1550"><em data-start="1376" data-end="1536">“With time, patience, and the financial support of Europe and, in particular, NATO, the original Borders from where this War started, is very much an option,”</em> Trump said.</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="1552" data-end="1760">The American leader emphasized that Russia has been waging a senseless war against Ukraine for over three and a half years. According to Trump, a <em><strong>“real military power”</strong></em> could have won it in less than a week.</p>
<blockquote>
<p data-start="1762" data-end="1844"><em data-start="1762" data-end="1829">“In fact, it is very much making them look like ‘a paper tiger,’”</em> Trump wrote.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 id="economic-pressure-on-russia-and-ukraines-opportunities" data-start="1846" data-end="1907">Economic pressure on Russia and Ukraine’s opportunities</h3>
<p data-start="1909" data-end="2109">He said that Ukraine will be able to restore its country to its previous state when residents of Moscow and all major Russian cities, towns, and regions realize what is really happening in this war.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_3"></div>
<p data-start="2111" data-end="2365">And when they understand that it is almost impossible to get gasoline due to extremely long queues and face all the other problems of a wartime economy, where most resources are spent fighting Ukraine, a country with a higher morale that only grows stronger.</p>
<p data-start="2367" data-end="2421">In reality, most Russians still support the war against Ukraine. They are enduring poverty and sanctions, yet are mobilizing to serve on the front lines. </p>
<h3 id="the-us-and-nato-support" data-start="2423" data-end="2448">The US and NATO support</h3>
<p data-start="2450" data-end="2601">The US president noted that Russian President Vladimir Putin faces massive economic difficulties. He believes that now is the time for Ukraine to act.</p>
<p data-start="2603" data-end="2707">Trump said the US will continue to supply weapons to NATO <strong><em data-start="2661" data-end="2705">“for NATO to do what they want with them.”</em></strong></p>

          <div class="read-also">
          <div class="read-also__inner">
                          <h2 id="read-also" class="read-also__headline">
                Read also              </h2>
                        
            <ul class="read-also__list">
                        
                                  <li>
                                        
                                        
                      <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/23/isw-russia-dangles-nuclear-talks-to-extract-trump-concessions-on-war-in-ukraine/" target="_blank" class="read-also__title">
                        <h3 id="isw-russia-dangles-nuclear-talks-to-extract-trump-concessions-on-war-in-ukraine">ISW: Russia dangles nuclear talks to extract Trump concessions on war in Ukraine</h3>
                      </a>
                                      </li>
                  
                        
                                  <li>
                                        
                                        
                      <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/23/russia-claims-french-british-troops-arrived-in-odesa-to-target-transnistria-as-sandu-warns-of-moldova-based-assault-on-ukraine/" target="_blank" class="read-also__title">
                        <h3 id="russia-claims-french-british-troops-arrived-in-odesa-to-target-transnistria-as-sandu-warns-of-moldova-based-assault-on-ukraine">Russia claims French, British troops arrived in Odesa to target Transnistria as Sandu warns of Moldova-based assault on Ukraine</h3>
                      </a>
                                      </li>
                  
                          </ul>
          </div>
      </div>
    
