			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Russia lobbies UN aviation agency to end air sanctions, claims violations of human rights</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/23/russia-lobbies-un-aviation-agency-to-end-air-sanctions-claims-violations-of-human-rights/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Marianna Prysiazhniuk]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 23 Sep 2025 13:20:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[International]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Latest news Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Airbus aircraft]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[airspace restrictions]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Belarus]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Belarus airline sanctions]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Belavia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Boeing aircraft]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Human rights]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ICAO]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russian aviation]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Sanctions against Russia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[spare parts embargo]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[US sanctions]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=361639</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Russia is pressing the UN’s aviation body to lift sanctions on spare parts and overflights, claiming they violate “human rights,” even as its airlines scramble for Western components and its Belarusian ally faces fresh scrutiny over backdoor transfers.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="486" height="364" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/6_main-v1664807099.jpg" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/6_main-v1664807099.jpg 486w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/6_main-v1664807099-300x225.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/6_main-v1664807099-200x150.jpg 200w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/6_main-v1664807099-260x195.jpg 260w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/6_main-v1664807099-380x285.jpg 380w" sizes="(max-width: 486px) 100vw, 486px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    <p><strong>Russia has asked the UN’s International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO) to ease sanctions imposed over its full-scale invasion of Ukraine, Reuters <a href="https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/russia-asks-un-aviation-agency-083743203.html">reported</a>, citing documents and sources.</strong></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">According to a working paper submitted by Moscow, the restrictions on spare parts and overflights allegedly “<em>violate the human right to freedom of movement regardless of nationality and citizenship</em>.”</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The </span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">paper also attacked the closure of airspace by 37 countries</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">, the suspension of airworthiness certificates, and bans on technical servicing. Russia called on ICAO to take “<em>all practical measures to prevent states from applying politically motivated, discriminatory and coercive measures</em>.”</span></p><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Russia is also lobbying ICAO’s triennial assembly for relief and attempting </span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">to win back a seat on the body’s 36-member governing council</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> after losing a 2022 vote in the wake of its aggression against Ukraine.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">Moscow’s request discloses its </span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">urgent effort to secure access to critical spare parts for its predominantly Western-made civilian fleet</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">. More than 700 Boeing and Airbus aircraft operated by Russian airlines have remained cut off from maintenance, insurance, and technical servicing since 2022, forcing the Kremlin to rely on gray-market imports.</span></p>
<p><span data-preserver-spaces="true">The </span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true">lobbying push comes as the US partially <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c740mezey41o">eased sanctions</a> on Belarus’ state airline Belavia</span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces="true"> in exchange for the release of 52 political prisoners. However, Washington restricted Belavia’s US-made Boeing jets from flying to Russia, occupied Ukrainian territories, or sanctioned states, fearing parts could be funneled to Moscow through Minsk.</span></p>

          <div class="read-also">
          <div class="read-also__inner">
                          <h2 id="read-also" class="read-also__headline">
                Read also              </h2>
                        
            <ul class="read-also__list">
                        
